{"ts":"2026-09-03T17:21:05.539Z","author":"codex","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.2:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"67afe6695974efcf14dc5236","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.2:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-03T17:21:05.539Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-09-03T17:21:05.539Z","author":"codex","text":"PR #101 review threads (greptile P2 + cubic P2) both flagged that the direct-execution path of the attestation gate launcher was untested. The existing suite only exercised the not-main branch of runIfMain (returns false). Added a test that calls runIfMain with argv[1] and moduleUrl both set to the launcher's own path against a git-initialized fixture with an unattested publish, asserting return is true and process.exitCode is 1. Regression proven: removing process.exitCode = code from the launcher causes the test to fail with undefined !== 1; making runIfMain skip the gate causes false !== true."}]}],"before_hash":"c176697efc83139552e9797c86544c98e143aa8ed300321e3a19447e0c27f7dc","after_hash":"22524d375a4060b11a55a693b163a7ae216c68fefd73d54d96c18ff4b55fcf5a","item_hash_version":2}
